import ../../helpers/driver.dl

appearance page appearance:
    maximum width is 800
    padding is 20
    gap is 24
appearance grid appearance:
    columns are 2
    stack below 600
    gap is 20
appearance text appearance:
    font size is 20
    line spacing is 1.5
appearance link appearance:
    use text appearance
    padding is 8
    background is UI ink 230 240 250
    corner radius is 6

appearance root appearance:
    background is UI ink 250 250 249

document responsive page using root appearance:
    region "page" using page appearance:
        region "columns" using grid appearance:
            paragraph "A paragraph that wraps across multiple lines." using text appearance
            link "Go to documentation" to "/wiki/" using link appearance
        paragraph "A long document." using text appearance
        surface "scene" using tall appearance

appearance tall appearance:
    height is 900

set instance to an instance of responsive page
bind (the control labeled "scene" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "paint nothing $") for event 1
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 1000 by 600 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition view's layout's appearance's filled reporting "The document appearance was not applied"
set page to the UI layout labeled "page" in (view's layout)
set columns to the UI layout labeled "columns" in (view's layout)
set link to the UI layout labeled "Go to documentation" in (view's layout)
require condition (columns's first's appearance's background's red = 250) reporting "Transparent content lost the background beneath it"
set the destination of "Go to documentation" in (the address of instance) to (the string form of "/wiki/terms.html")
require condition ((the UI value for (link's node) in (the address of instance))'s destination = "/wiki/terms.html") reporting "A link did not retain its updated destination"
require condition ((page's bounds' width = 800.0) and (page's bounds' x = 100.0)) reporting "The document's maximum width was not centered"
require condition (link's bounds' x > columns's first's bounds' x) reporting "Desktop columns were stacked"
set view's width to 390
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((link's bounds' x = columns's first's bounds' x) and (link's bounds' y > columns's first's bounds' y)) reporting "Mobile columns did not stack"
require condition (columns's first's lines' next != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text line)) reporting "Paragraph text was not wrapped"
set view's selection's anchor source to the address of (columns's first's text source)
set view's selection's caret source to view's selection's anchor source
set view's selection's anchor to 2
set view's selection's caret to 40
set selected to the selected UI text in (the address of view)
require condition (selected = "paragraph that wraps across multiple l") reporting "Soft wrapping inserted text into the selection"
set view's width to 1000
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the selected UI text in (the address of view)) = selected) reporting "Reflow moved the selection to another source offset"
queue UI input of kind 5 key 0 at 0.0 450.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's layout's scroll target = 450.0) reporting "The document did not accept wheel scrolling"
require condition ((the selected UI text in (the address of view)) = selected) reporting "Scrolling changed the selected text"
set view's layout's scroll position to 450.0
set view's height to 2000
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((view's layout's scroll position = 0.0) and (view's layout's scroll target = 0.0)) reporting "Growing the viewport left the document scrolled past its end"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Document width, responsive columns, wrapping and scrolling work."

to paint nothing {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    ignore painting
